{"id": "q0072", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 171000483, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "Timothy has three times the number of pens that George owns. Sarah has half as many pens as Timothy. If George has 18 pens, how many pens does Sarah have?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0072.wav", "input_sha256": "52df4602799567f8ef08e13b7e1438b895224e3197853c77ab4d09a0a4d3e5f3", "input_samples": 196000, "input_s": 12.25, "n_real_chunks": 13, "score": 0.0386, "act": 0.9984, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so if George has 18 pens and Tim othy has three times that number, then Timothy has 3 times 18 pens. That' s 54 pen s for Timothy. Sarah has half as many pens as Timothy, so we take half of 5 4. Half of 54 is 27. So Sarah has 2 7 pens.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 12, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 19, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0072_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "2701f2eb1977b36f5a47684ba294ab8997c487cf56be54e3d7e9881325ff3f26", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 19.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.054, 1.096, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.053, 2.096, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.055, 3.098, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.056, 4.101, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.056, 5.102, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.056, 6.101, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.056, 7.101, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1