{"id": "q0183", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4218160333, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "A 37-year-old man with type 1 diabetes mellitus is admitted to the hospital because of inadequate control of his glucose concentrations for the past 2 months. Despite his poor control, he demands that he be discharged. He reports that he has had a 3-month history of fatigue, irritability, and feelings of hopelessness. He says that he has been noncompliant with his diabetic regimen, adding, \"Sometimes I forget.\" He has been avoiding his family and friends because he is not in the mood to see them but admits that he is lonely. He did not get out of bed for 2 days, which prompted his wife to call an ambulance and have him admitted to the hospital. Prior to admission to the hospital, his only medication was insulin, although he often missed doses. He does not drink alcohol. He is 168 cm (5 ft 6 in) tall and weighs 100 kg (220 lb); BMI is 36 kg/m2 . His temperature is 37°C (98.6°F), pulse is 68/min, respirations are 18/min, and blood pressure is 150/85 mm Hg. Physical examination shows no abnormalities. On mental status examination, he is tired and has a restricted affect. There is no evidence of suicidal ideation. Cognition is intact. His fasting serum glucose concentration is 120 mg/dL. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management? \n\nA. Insist on hospitalization against the patient's wishes\nB. Initiate insulin therapy immediately\nC. Begin a psychotherapy session\nD. Seek a court order to appoint a legal guardian\nE. Schedule neuropsychological testing\nF. Start a diet and exercise regimen\nG. Prescribe medication for depression\nH. Conduct a full body physical examination\nI. Adhere to the patient's wishes on the condition that he agree to home nursing care\nJ. Adhere to the patient's wishes and discuss home-care options\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0183.wav", "input_sha256": "d1eaa7f0e89064c1dfc09cde7c222d8dd0cbf93f40f6497fdb0181f360222b2c", "input_samples": 1913800, "input_s": 119.612, "n_real_chunks": 120, "score": 0.7567, "act": 0.9991, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so let's break this down. First off, his BMI is 3 6 kg/m 2. That'", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 54, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 5, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0183_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "9b2c5d635488b193c049e72f36c22106ec1ecbfa58703a0ffbeb7030bffe68b7", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 5.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.052, 1.094, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.055, 2.098, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.055, 3.098, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.055, 4.099, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.055, 5.099, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.056, 6.101, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.055, 7.099, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.056, 8.1, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.056, 9.101, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.058, 10.102, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.057, 11.101, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.058, 12.102, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.056, 13.102, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.058, 14.106, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.058, 15.103, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.058, 16.102, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.058, 17.102, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.059, 18.103, 1, 0, 0], [18, 1, 19.0, 19.059, 19.104, 1, 0, 0], [19, 1, 20.0, 20.059, 20.105, 1, 0, 0], [20, 1, 21.0, 21.059, 21.103, 1, 0, 0